<title>USA: STV Group Q2 shr rises to $0.10.</title>
<headline>STV Group Q2 shr rises to $0.10.</headline>
<dateline>DOUGLASSVILLE, Pa. 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Amounts in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>				Three Months Ended  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>				   March 31,		March 31,</p>
<p>			     1997	 1996	 1997	 1996</p>
<p> Total revenues	$22,311    $23,502    $45,047    $46,485</p>
<p>Less pass-through costs</p>
<p>			     4,130	5,714	8,743     10,693</p>
<p>Net engineering revenues</p>
<p>  for work performed  18,181     17,788     36,304     35,792</p>
<p> Net income		  183	   71	  341	  174</p>
<p>Earnings per common share</p>
<p>				 .10	  .04	  .18	  .10</p>
<p>Average common shares</p>
<p>and equivalents  1,902,851  1,868,225  1,900,778  1,859,910</p>
<p>NOTE: The start of the New Jersey Transit Hudson-Bergen</p>
<p>light rail project in the second quarter for fiscal 1997</p>
<p>contributed to the company's improved earnings. The second</p>
<p>quarter of fiscal 1996 was negatively impacted by severe</p>
<p>winter conditions in the Northeast.</p>
<p>Full company name is STV Group Inc.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
